page cmd_script {
  title = "vmlab script"
  chapter_header "vmlab script" {
    kicker       = "Commands · reference"
    reading_time = "3 min read"
    updated      = "2026-09-02"
    version      = "vmlab 0.9"
  }

  p <<DOC
    `vmlab script` runs an ad-hoc [wscript](guide_scripting) file against the
    lab of the current directory. The script runs inside the lab daemon, with
    the same `lab` binding a `provision {}` block or an event handler gets,
    and its output streams back to the terminal as it is produced.
  DOC

  code sh { source = "vmlab script <SCRIPT>" }

  table {
    rows:
      | "Option" | "Meaning" |
      | "`<SCRIPT>`" | "Script path, relative to the lab root." |
      | "`-h`, `--help`" | "Print help." |
  }

  p <<DOC
    The path is resolved against the lab root, the directory holding
    `vmlab.wcl`, not against the shell's directory, so the same command works
    from any subdirectory of the lab. The command checks the file exists
    before it asks anything and refuses with `script <path> not found under
    <root>` when it does not. It then starts the supervisor and the lab
    daemon if they are not running, sends the `run` request, and prints each
    chunk of output as it arrives. Machines the script touches must already
    be up; the script itself can start them through the
    [Lab API](ref_ws_lab).
  DOC

  p <<DOC
    The console runs declared playbooks and never a scratch script, so
    `script` is reachable only from the CLI: the file comes from the caller's
    disk and its output belongs to the terminal that ran it.
  DOC

  code sh { source = <<'SRC'
cd examples/ad-lab
vmlab up
vmlab script scripts/collect-dumps.ws
SRC
  }

  p <<DOC
    Exit status is 0 when the script completes. A script that raises, or a
    call inside it that fails, ends the run with `failed` (1). A missing file
    or a daemon that does not start exits 1 before any request is sent.
  DOC
}
